  ("5.1 General remarks about Spanish adjectives" 0.09195 0.71664 0.37356 0.39781 0.39781 0.02425 0.00789 0.2972 0.0394 "UFSJES+Univers-Bold" 0.0201 t nil 0 "UFSJES+Univers" nil)
  ("(a) Nearly all Spanish adjectives agree with nouns and pronouns in number, and many also" 0.09195 0.90814 0.40479 0.42127 0.42127 0.01648 0.00482 0.2748 0.0225 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 0 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" nil)
  ("agree in gender. They therefore either have two forms, e.g. natural/naturales, or four, e.g. bueno/" 0.09195 0.90803 0.42129 0.43777 0.43777 0.01648 0.00482 0.2977 0.0461 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 0 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" nil)
  ("buena/buenos/buenas. A few, e.g. macho ‘male’, violeta ‘violet’, are invariable in form." 0.09195 0.78928 0.43778 0.45427 0.45427 0.01648 0.00482 0.3601 0.1703 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 0 "UFSJES+Palatino-Italic" nil)
  ("(b) The position of adjectives is a subtle question, the difference between un problema difícil and" 0.09195 0.90805 0.46648 0.48296 0.48296 0.01648 0.00482 0.3076 0.0246 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 0 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" nil)
  ("un difícil problema ‘a diffi cult problem’ being virtually untranslatable in English." 0.09195 0.76526 0.48297 0.49946 0.49946 0.01648 0.00482 0.3388 0.0214 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 0 "UFSJES+Palatino-Italic" nil)
  ("(c) It is necessary to distinguish ‘descriptive’ adjectives (adjetivos califi cativos), e.g. ‘a big book’," 0.09195 0.90806 0.51166 0.52815 0.52815 0.01648 0.00482 0.2636 0.0214 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 0 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" nil)
  ("‘a blond girl’ from ‘relational’ adjectives (adjetivos relacionales), e.g. ‘a nuclear power-station’, ‘a" 0.09195 0.90805 0.52816 0.54465 0.54465 0.01648 0.00482 0.2898 0.0150 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 0 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" nil)
  ("pedestrian crossing’. See Glossary for defi nitions." 0.09195 0.5009 0.54466 0.56115 0.56115 0.01648 0.00482 0.2932 0.0803 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 0 "UFSJES+Palatino-Italic" nil)
  ("(d) Many, but not all, Spanish adjectives become nouns if a determiner (see Glossary) is added:" 0.09195 0.90794 0.57335 0.58984 0.58984 0.01648 0.00482 0.3352 0.0246 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 0 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" nil)
  ("joven/estas jóvenes ‘young’/‘these young women’; see 5.9b. Nouns can also occasionally be used" 0.09195 0.90808 0.58985 0.60633 0.60633 0.01648 0.00482 0.3005 0.0849 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 0 "UFSJES+Palatino-Italic" nil)
  ("like adjectives, as in ella es más mujer que Julia ‘she’s more (of a) woman than Julia’ (or ‘more femi-" 0.09195 0.90818 0.60635 0.62283 0.62283 0.01648 0.00482 0.4071 0.0311 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 0 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" nil)
  ("nine’); see 5.9a." 0.09195 0.22056 0.62285 0.63933 0.63933 0.01648 0.00482 0.3028 0.0538 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 0 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" nil)
  ("However, adjectives are formed in unpredictable ways from nouns, e.g. automóvil – automovilístico," 0.09195 0.90801 0.65154 0.66802 0.66802 0.01648 0.00482 0.3844 0.0829 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 0 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" nil)
  ("metal – metálico, leche ‘milk’ lechal, lechoso and lácteo." 0.09195 0.52529 0.66804 0.68452 0.68452 0.01648 0.00482 0.3548 0.0428 "UFSJES+Palatino-Italic" 0.0136 nil t 0 "UFSJES+Palatino-Italic" nil)
  ("(e) Some adjectives can be used with object pronouns and the verb ser: me es fácil ‘it’s easy" 0.09195 0.90809 0.69673 0.71321 0.71321 0.01648 0.00482 0.2677 0.0226 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 0 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" nil)
  ("for me’, nos son imprescindibles ‘they’re indispensable to us’; but most cannot. See 14.6.3 for" 0.09197 0.9081 0.71322 0.72971 0.72971 0.01648 0.00482 0.2809 0.0247 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 0 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" nil)
  ("discussion." 0.09197 0.18712 0.72972 0.74621 0.74621 0.01648 nil 0.2399 0.0951 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 0 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" nil)
  ("(f) Adjectival participles ending in -ante, -iente, e.g. vinculante ‘binding’, preocupante ‘worrying’," 0.09197 0.90808 0.75841 0.7749 0.7749 0.01648 0.00482 0.3130 0.0203 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 0 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" nil)
  ("are discussed under participles at 23.6." 0.09199 0.42051 0.77491 0.7914 0.7914 0.01648 0.00482 0.2824 0.0261 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 0 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" nil)
  ("(g) The gerund in -ndo is a verb form and must not be used as an adjective: una muñeca que anda" 0.09199 0.9082 0.8036 0.82009 0.82009 0.01648 0.00482 0.3213 0.0235 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 0 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" nil)
  ("or una muñeca andante ‘a walking doll’, not una muñeca andando ‘a doll walking’. For two excep-" 0.09199 0.90815 0.8201 0.83659 0.83659 0.01648 0.00482 0.3221 0.0181 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 0 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" nil)
  ("tions to this rule, see 5.3. For a discussion of the Gerund see Chapter 24." 0.09199 0.7008 0.8366 0.85308 0.85308 0.01648 0.00482 0.3197 0.0418 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 0 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" nil)
  ("(h) Spanish adverbs are invariable in form, even when they look like adjectives: los teléfonos" 0.09199 0.90816 0.86529 0.88177 0.88177 0.01648 0.00482 0.2655 0.0246 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 0 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" nil)
